WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.800
The sync is the kit's design.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.755
It reads the tenant's
settings catalog policies,

3
00:00:04.755 --> 00:00:08.522
through the list call Learn's
Graph beta reference documents,

4
00:00:08.522 --> 00:00:12.437
normalizes both sides, and gives
each library policy one action.

5
00:00:12.437 --> 00:00:14.426
Create: it isn't in the tenant.

6
00:00:14.426 --> 00:00:20.375
No change: the same settings, description,
platform, technology and scope tags.

7
00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:24.862
Drift: it differs, and the row
names each setting that changed.

8
00:00:24.862 --> 00:00:28.388
Duplicate: two tenant policies
have the library's name.

9
00:00:28.388 --> 00:00:30.550
Drift and duplicate exit two.

10
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:34.060
Without the apply option,
the sync is a dry run:

11
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:37.475
it signs in with read
only, and sends only GET.

12
00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:40.135
With apply, it signs in with read-write,

13
00:00:40.135 --> 00:00:43.738
POSTs each create, reads it
back and compares again.

14
00:00:43.738 --> 00:00:47.029
And it writes nothing at all
if the lint has a finding,

15
00:00:47.029 --> 00:00:49.250
or any policy is drift or duplicate.

16
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.400
It never sends PATCH or DELETE,
although Learn documents both.

17
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.281
A policy that differs from Git
is a decision for a person, and,

18
00:00:57.281 --> 00:01:02.180
in this workbook's guidance, a change
becomes a new version under a new name.
